* Hermetic ngspice init for sim/oscillator-core.
*
* Every run_*.sh in this directory copies this file into the scratch
* directory it runs ngspice from, so a run does NOT depend on whether
* $HOME/.spiceinit exists (the PDK ships libs.tech/ngspice/install.py, which
* symlinks one into $HOME; a cold-start checkout on a machine where that was
* never run must still reproduce the committed numbers).
*
* ngbehavior=hsa is the compatibility mode the PDK's own .spiceinit sets, and
* is what its model libraries are written against. Here it IS load-bearing,
* for the same reason design/.spiceinit says it is: the netlist under test
* instantiates the PDK's own npn13G2v, cap_cmim and sg13_hv_svaricap
* subcircuits, whose model cards use HSPICE-style constructs (.if/.else inside
* .subckt, expression-valued .model parameters) that ngspice only accepts in
* this mode. Without it ngspice prints "Note: No compatibility mode
* selected!" and the varactor bank does not resolve -- see klt-sim/README.md,
* where exactly that failure is the reproduction of one of the two tool gaps
* this experiment filed upstream.
*
* run_method_check.sh copies it too, even though its synthetic deck uses only
* ngspice-native behavioural sources and does not need the mode: the method
* check exists to validate the SAME extractor the PDK-dependent sweep uses,
* so it runs under the same ngspice configuration rather than quietly
* diverging from it.
set ngbehavior=hsa
